special_abilities:
  - { name: "Commune with Spirits", description: "Special ability 1 (printed 181). To find and speak with spirits or any supernatural being the Angakoq enters a trance and releases an Astral Form. In that form all lesser and most greater demons, spirits and supernatural beings can see and talk with the Shaman, each understands the other, and they will not attack unless attacked first. Nothing obliges them to answer, be truthful or cooperate." }
  - { name: "Recognize Supernatural Shapechangers", description: "Special ability 2 (printed 181). Base skill 30% +5% per level of experience. Spots werebeasts, vampires, Faerie Folk and similar shapechangers from an animal acting out of character, and can usually tell the likely race or true identity. Recognises a werebeast in both human and animal form; werebeasts do not automatically treat the Angakoq as an enemy and often speak frankly with one." }
  - { name: "Psionic Powers of the Angakoq", description: "Special ability 3 (printed 181). On becoming a Shaman the character gains Exorcism, Increase Healing, Psychic Diagnosis, Psychic Surgery, Clairvoyance, See Aura, See the Invisible and Mind Block, whether psychic before or not. A character who was already psychic loses four original powers, which these replace. The book prints no I.S.P. for the class; record I.S.P. by hand as the G.M. rules." }
  - { name: "Ley Line Healing/Rejuvenation", description: "Special ability 4 (printed 181-182). Resting on a ley line for several days doubles the rate of natural healing. Once every 48 hours the Angakoq can also heal at once: after 15+1D6 minutes of meditation seated on a ley line, 2D6 Hit Points and 2D6 S.D.C. are restored." }
  - { name: "Cast Magic Spells", description: "Special ability 5 (printed 182). The Angakoq''s own spells are Globe of Daylight, Tongues, See the Invisible, Sense Evil, Sense Magic, Second Sight, Chameleon, Repel Animals, Cure Minor Disorders, Heal Wounds, Purification (food/water), Spoil (food/water) and Sickness, plus the knowledge to create Inuit amulets and talismans. P.P.E. is the P.E. attribute number +2D6 per level of experience. Every other spell on the sheet belongs to the Tornaq." }
  - { name: "The Tornaq: the Spirit Bear", description: "Special ability 6 (printed 182-183). Within 72 hours of becoming a Shaman the Angakoq is joined for life by a spirit guardian in the shape of a bear, usually a Polar Bear, with the attributes and abilities of the normal animal. It is a Mega-Damage creature with M.D.C. equal to the Angakoq''s P.P.E. +100, regenerating 6D6 M.D.C. per hour, and a P.P.E. reserve of 1D4x100+150 that only its Shaman can draw on (up to half) to cast his own spells, the Tornaq''s spells, or to make amulets and talismans. It finds food, tracks animals and defends the Shaman; it never fights in its own defence, only to protect the Shaman or carry out a command, and will fight to the death unless sent away. The Shaman can will it to vanish only if it is truly about to be destroyed (typically at 20-25% of its M.D.C.); it returns once the Shaman is out of danger and alone or among friends. Through the bear the Shaman can also perform great healing, sway the weather a little and keep Sedna the Sea Hag calm; she will not harm an Angakoq. If the Tornaq dies it and its magic are gone for good and the Shaman is disgraced, left with only skills, psionics and the thirteen spells of his own. Each amulet made permanently drains the Tornaq of 10 P.P.E. and each talisman or special item of 20; at half its original P.P.E. all its powers, abilities and M.D.C. are halved." }
  - { name: "Tornaq Spells", description: "Special ability 6, continued (printed 183). Cast by the Shaman, never the bear, by channelling the Tornaq''s P.P.E. reserve; the same spell cannot be cast more than twice in 24 hours. Energy Disruption, Superhuman Strength, Swim as a Fish (superior), Impervious to Cold, Eyes of the Bear (same as Eyes of the Wolf), Armor of Ithan, Turn Dead, Commune with Spirits, Exorcism, Constrain Being, Banishment, Control/Enslave Entity, Blind, Mute, Minor Curse, Remove Curse, Negate Magic, Dispel Magic Barrier, Stone to Flesh, Restoration, Anti-Magic Cloud, Amulet, Talisman, Summon and Control Animals, Summon Fog and Calm Storms, plus Aura of Power, Mystic Fulcrum, Fist of Fury, Frostblade, Tame Beast and Restore Life from Rifts Federation of Magic. All are lost if the Tornaq dies." }
  - { name: "Initiative against the Supernatural", description: "Special O.C.C. bonus (printed 183): +3 on initiative, but only when fighting the supernatural. Not applied by the sheet." }
  - { name: "Inuit Amulets & Talismans", description: "Starts with two amulets and two talismans (printed 183). More can be made as the G.M. allows; as a rule of thumb one more amulet every three levels (3, 6, 9, 12 and 15) and one more talisman every other level (2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12 and 14). Making one always needs the Tornaq''s P.P.E. or a ley line nexus at a time of power. Only the Angakoq or the person he gives it to can use one; no more than one amulet and one talisman can be worn at a time; after one is taken off, no other can be worn for 24 hours; and the magic ends when the maker or the recipient dies. Most have 60 M.D.C." }
